-- Regression test for lexical section scoping — FIX D, order-independence of
-- a type-directed reference across a differently-typed rebinding (spec §12).
--
-- A section binds x to a STRING and refers to x in a NUMBER position. A
-- sibling or descendant section binds a NUMBER x. Under the per-type rule
-- (spec §3.3.4 step 4) the differently-typed off-ancestry binding stays
-- visible to type-directed resolution, so `x PLUS 1` resolves to the NUMBER x
-- and evaluates to 3 — whether that binding is placed ABOVE or BELOW the
-- reference. The first cut of FIX D dropped the not-yet-inferred candidate
-- outright, which kept the ABOVE order at 3 but turned the BELOW order into a
-- type error at the reference. A not-yet-inferred candidate is now DEFERRED
-- instead: consulted only when the ancestry does not resolve the reference.
--
-- This fixture pins order-independence, not the design of the flat fallback;
-- see the dated note under spec §3.3.4 for that rule as shipped.

-- 1. Descendant, rebinding BELOW the reference.
§ a
x MEANS "s"
f MEANS x PLUS 1              -- 3: §§ b's NUMBER x
§§ b
x MEANS 2

-- 2. Descendant, rebinding ABOVE the reference.
§ c
y MEANS "s"
§§ d
y MEANS 2
§§ e
g MEANS y PLUS 1              -- 3: §§ d's NUMBER y

-- 3. Sibling, rebinding BELOW the reference.
§ m
z MEANS "s"
h MEANS z PLUS 1              -- 3: § n's NUMBER z
§ n
z MEANS 2

-- 4. Sibling, rebinding ABOVE the reference.
§ o
w MEANS 2
§ p
w MEANS "s"
k MEANS w PLUS 1              -- 3: § o's NUMBER w

#EVAL a.f       -- 3
#EVAL c.e.g     -- 3
#EVAL m.h       -- 3
#EVAL p.k       -- 3
